  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "---\ndescription: \"A DeepSeek Harness Web plugin for AI conversation graphs, research topics, and source-linked Knowledge Cards. Explore capabilities, check compatibility, and install the research workbench.\"\nkind: \"package-bundle\"\n---\n\n<a id=\"dsh-research-graph--研图\"></a>"
    },
    {
      "section": "DSH Research Graph",
      "text": "[](https://github.com/benz-ai-x/dsh-research-graph/actions/workflows/ci.yml) [](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@benz-ai-x/dsh-research-graph) [](LICENSE)\n\n**English** | [简体中文](README.zh.md)"
    },
    {
      "section": "DSH Research Graph",
      "text": "An independently maintained, open-source **AI research workbench plugin** for [DeepSeek Harness (DSH)](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness), running inside **DSH Web**. Organize conversations into research topics and traceable Knowledge Cards for product research, technical research, and ongoing knowledge management."
    },
    {
      "section": "Capability map",
      "text": "```mermaid\n---\nconfig:\n  flowchart:\n    nodeSpacing: 16"
    },
    {
      "section": "Workbench screenshot",
      "text": "<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"docs/assets/readme/research-workbench.png\">\n    <img src=\"docs/assets/readme/research-workbench.png\" alt=\"Research workbench linking source discussions, Knowledge Cards, and follow-up research, with conclusions, revisions, and source links in the reader\" width=\"100%\" />\n  </a>\n</p>\n\nVersion 0.2.1-rc.3 with demo data. Click the image for the full-resolution screenshot.\n\n<a id=\"features\"></a>\n<a id=\"what-it-adds\"></a>"
    },
    {
      "section": "Key capabilities",
      "text": "| Capability | What you can do |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Research graph** | Organize discussions, inspect branches and merges; drag, collapse, and relayout; cards show turn counts and the inspector reports Session stats |\n| **Own sidebar with Workspace folders** | Replaces the official sidebar with this package's copy and adds user-created folders inside each Workspace: create/rename/delete from the workspace menu, drag Sessions in or out, native row menus everywhere. Uninstalling the plugin restores the official sidebar |\n| **Source tracing** | Search discussion text and return to the exact original turns |\n| **Knowledge capture** | Save conclusions, conditions, and open questions; edit through new revisions |\n| **AI analysis** | Extract selected discussion and compare 2–3 materials; review before saving |\n| **Follow-up research** | Start from a historical turn or chosen card revision, retaining the materials used |\n| **Tasks and delivery** | Inspect existing subagent records and export Markdown research results |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Key capabilities",
      "text": "<a id=\"compatibility\"></a>\n<a id=\"dsh-and-agent-presets\"></a>"
    },
    {
      "section": "Key facts",
      "text": "| Item | Details |\n| --- | --- |\n| Plugin release | [0.2.2-rc.1](https://github.com/benz-ai-x/dsh-research-graph/releases/tag/v0.2.2-rc.1), npm `next` |\n| Required Host | **DSH 0.2.2-rc.1 · Web**, Node.js `>=24.9.0` |\n| Data | Research records and Workspace folders live on the DSH Host; view preferences and working positions stay in the browser, and Topic arrangements require explicit saving |\n| Model calls | Browsing, manual capture, and export make no model call; AI generation and new discussions use models on demand |\n| Agent capabilities | DSH provides models, tools, presets, and agent execution; this plugin includes no preset or Agent Team launcher. [Details](docs/user-guide.md#dsh-and-agent-presets) |\n| Stack and license | TypeScript · React · [MIT](LICENSE) |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Key facts",
      "text": "<a id=\"install\"></a>"
    },
    {
      "section": "Quick start",
      "text": "Requires **DSH 0.2.2-rc.1** (Node.js `>=24.9.0`), with both `dsh` and `pnpm` on your `PATH`. Stop any running `dsh web`, then run:\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add @benz-ai-x/dsh-research-graph@0.2.2-rc.1\ndsh web\n```\n\nOpen the login URL printed in the terminal, enter a **non-blank Session**, and select **Research Graph**: read a source → save knowledge → continue the discussion. See [installation options](docs/user-guide.md#install) if you run DSH through `npx` or from source."
    },
    {
      "section": "Quick start",
      "text": "<a id=\"installable-versions\"></a>"
    },
    {
      "section": "Installable versions",
      "text": "Every npm release of the current package name, with its required DSH Host (taken from each release's pinned `@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm` peer). Install a specific one with `dsh plugin --profile web add @benz-ai-x/dsh-research-graph@<version>`:"
    },
    {
      "section": "Installable versions",
      "text": "| Plugin release | Required DSH | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `0.2.2-rc.1` | `0.2.2-rc.1` | Current release — first adaptation of this DSH line; requires Node.js `>=24.9.0`; npm `next` |\n| `0.2.1-rc.5.2` | `0.2.1-rc.5` | **Breaking change**: replaces the official sidebar with the vendored copy and Workspace folders (supersedes sidebar categories; old category data stays dormant) |\n| `0.2.1-rc.5.1` | `0.2.1-rc.5` | Native-style sidebar categories and footer view switching |\n| `0.2.1-rc.5` | `0.2.1-rc.5` | First adaptation of this DSH line |\n| `0.2.1-rc.4` | `0.2.1-rc.4` | First adaptation of this DSH line |\n| `0.2.1-rc.3.1` | `0.2.1-rc.3` | Workspace-owned sidebar categories |\n| `0.2.1-rc.3` | `0.2.1-rc.3` | First release of this DSH line |\n| `0.2.1-rc.1` | `0.2.1-rc.1` | |\n| `0.2.1-alpha.5` | `0.2.1-alpha.5` | |\n| `0.2.1-alpha.2.1` | `0.2.1-alpha.2` | Merge model selection and rename fix |\n| `0.2.1-alpha.2` | `0.2.1-alpha.2` | |\n| `0.2.1-alpha.1` | `0.2.1-alpha.1` | |\n| `0.2.0-rc.2.1` | `0.2.0-rc.2` | Same-line revision (workbench design refresh) |\n| `0.2.0-rc.2` | `0.2.0-rc.2` | First release of that DSH line |\n| `0.1.7-rc.2` | `0.1.7-rc.2` | |\n| `0.1.7-rc.1` | `0.1.7-rc.1` | |\n"
    },
    {
      "section": "Installable versions",
      "text": "Releases up to `0.1.5-rc.1` were also published under the previous package name `@benz-ai-x/dsh-client-ui-session-graph`, whose earlier `0.1.1`–`0.1.6` line predates the DSH-aligned release policy. A release loads only on its pinned DSH Host (profile boot enforces the exact peer check), so pick the row matching your DSH installation."
    },
    {
      "section": "Docs and support",
      "text": "[User guide](docs/user-guide.md) · [Troubleshooting](docs/user-guide.md#troubleshooting) · [Development and release](docs/development.md) · [Release acceptance](docs/reviews/release-0.2.2-rc.1.md) · [Report an issue](https://github.com/benz-ai-x/dsh-research-graph/issues)"
    }
